  "body": "It would be very helpful if the `user_mapping_provider` of `OIDC` would support the mapping of a bit more complex data structure.\r\n\r\nFor instance if the returned data would not be `user.id` but `user.data.id`.\r\n\r\nSo instead of ...\r\n```\r\n    user_mapping_provider:\r\n      config:\r\n        subject_claim: \"id\"\r\n        localpart_template: \"{{ user.id }}\" \r\n        display_name_template: \"{{ user.name }}\"\r\n        email_template: \"{{ user.email }}\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nit would require to be mapped like this...\r\n\r\n```\r\n    user_mapping_provider:\r\n      config:\r\n        subject_claim: \"id\"\r\n        localpart_template: \"{{ user.data.id }}\" \r\n        display_name_template: \"{{ user.data.name }}\"\r\n        email_template: \"{{ user.data.email }}\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis would be more flexible.\r\n",
